\label{thm:random}
Let $\varepsilon>0$, let $\mu$ be any i.i.d.\ strictly positive idea-size law, $Y:=(1+H)^{-\varepsilon}$, $y_j:=\mathbb{E} Y^j\in(0,1)$, and $\bar\zeta:=\kappa A_0^\varepsilon\zeta$. Then
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\alph*)]
\item $\bar\zeta\overset{d}{=}e+Y\bar\zeta'$ with $e\sim\operatorname{Exp}(1)$, $Y$ and $\bar\zeta'\overset d=\bar\zeta$ independent;
\item $\mathbb{E}\bar\zeta^{\,m}=m!\big/\prod_{j=1}^m(1-y_j)$ for $m\in\mathbb{N}$;
\item $\operatorname{CV}(\bar\zeta)^2=\dfrac{2(1-y_1)}{1-y_2}-1$.
\end{enumerate}

\label{thm:race}
As $t\uparrow T^\ast$:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item if $\lambda_S<\varepsilon$, then $S(t)\to S(T^\ast)<\infty$;
\item if $\lambda_S\ge\varepsilon$, then $S(t)\to\infty$, and
\[
\frac{S(t)}{A(t)}\longrightarrow
\begin{cases}
0,& \varepsilon_S<\varepsilon,\\[2pt]
\mathcal R(\theta):=\Big(\dfrac{c_S(\theta k)^{\lambda_S}}{c((1-\theta)k)^{\lambda}}\Big)^{1/\beta_S},&\varepsilon_S=\varepsilon,\\[8pt]
\infty,&\varepsilon_S>\varepsilon.
\end{cases}
\]
\end{enumerate}
Away from the critical equality $\varepsilon_S=\varepsilon$, changing a fixed allocation share $\theta\in(0,1)$ changes constants and dates but not the asymptotic regime of the ratio $S/A$. At the critical equality the limit $\mathcal R(\theta)$ depends on $\theta$.
